Brian M. Dean <elzoog@yahoo.com> wrote:
> I know that part of the answer to this question is to make a .nethackrc 
> file in my home directory (I am running linux).  But here is specifically 
> what I want.
> 
> Whenever I start QT Nethack I always have to set the following options:
> 
> under
> Game -> QT Settings:
> 
> Font: Large
> Width: 25
> Height: 40
> 
> under 
> Game -> Options
> number_pad (1=on)
> 
> 
> It is pretty tedious to have to set these options every time I run 
> nethack.  So what lines do I need to put in a .nethackrc file to have it 
> automatically set these options every time I play?

I haven't tested this (no Qt NetHack at hand), just looked at the
source code, but the following in ~/.nethackrc should work:


QT_TILEWIDTH=25
QT_TILEHEIGHT=40
QT_FONTSIZE=l
OPTIONS=number_pad:1


